        "Use a parcel worksheet with item weight, approximate dimensions, keep-or-remove packaging choice and compatibility notes. Then compare a consolidated plan with a split plan when the difference matters. Consider the risk of placing every item in one parcel as well as the price. If one shipment is delayed or damaged, the concentration is larger. There is no universal correct parcel count; a good spreadsheet makes the trade-off visible instead of treating consolidation as a magic discount."
